{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rx82dojMxJhj3BrHMPBRtS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n    26→        \"Courtiers\",\n    27→        \"Musicians\",\n    28→        \"Buffoons\",\n    29→        \"Improvisatori\",\n    30→        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n    31→        \"Beauty\"\n    32→      ],\n    33→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by sharp pains, profuse bleeding, and scarlet stains that isolate victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, castellated abbey, welding shut its iron gates to ensure total isolation. Inside, he hosts an extravagant masked ball across seven uniquely colored chambers, each lit by blood-red firelight filtering through stained glass windows, with a massive ebony clock in the black room whose hourly chimes halt the music and freeze the revelers in dread. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself—dripping in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask—causing terror and paralysis among the guests until Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through the chambers with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black room, revealing the figure to be empty; the plague has infiltrated the abbey, and one by one, all the revelers die as darkness and decay claim the entire estate.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\",\n    42→        \"the mummer\"\n    43→      ],\n    44→      \"role\": null,\n    45→      \"appearance\": null,\n    46→      \"personality\": null,\n    47→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    48→      \"descriptions\": [\n    49→        {\n    50→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a self-indulgent and defiant ruler who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a sealed abbey to escape the Red Death, hosting a lavish masked ball in a display of arrogance and denial. His actions—refusing to acknowledge the plague, mocking the suffering outside, and violently pursuing the figure of the Red Death—reveal a man consumed by hubris who ultimately dies in terror, confirming his fatal delusion and the futility of his attempt to evade death.\",\n    51→          \"source_position\": 1894,\n    52→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    53→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    54→        }\n    55→      ],\n    56→      \"relationships\": {},\n    57→      \"evidence\": [\n    58→        {\n    59→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero isolates himself and his courtiers in a sealed abbey to escape the plague\",\n    60→          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, castellated abbey, welding shut its iron gates to ensure total isolation.\",\n    61→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n    62→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    63→        },\n    64→        {\n    65→          \"statement\": \"He hosts an extravagant masked ball while the plague rages outside\",\n    66→          \"quote\": \"It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence.\",\n    67→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 1894\",\n    68→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    69→        },\n    70→        {\n    71→          \"statement\": \"He is enraged by the figure dressed as the Red Death\",\n    72→          \"quote\": \"Insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    73→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 11148\",\n    74→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    75→        },\n    76→        {\n    77→          \"statement\": \"He pursues the figure through all seven chambers with a dagger\",\n    78→          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n    79→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12389\",\n    80→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    81→        },\n    82→        {\n    83→          \"statement\": \"He collapses and dies upon confronting the figure in the black room\",\n    84→          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n    85→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12980\",\n    86→          \"confidence\": \"high\