"first_position\": 11611,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"glossary\": null,\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"structure\": {\n      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n      \"has_titles\": false,\n      \"has_parts\": false,\n      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n    },\n    \"plot_summary\": {\n      \"plot_summary\": \"The story begins in the midst of a terrifying epidemic known as the Red Death, a merciless plague that spreads rapidly through the land, marked by violent symptoms and fatal scarlet stains. Amid the chaos and despair, Prince Prospero, a man of immense wealth and arrogance, chooses to defy the inevitable by sealing himself and a thousand courtiers within the fortified walls of his secluded, castellated abbey. With iron gates welded shut and the outside world cut off, he attempts to escape the plague’s reach by indulging in extravagant pleasures, hosting a lavish masked ball that spans seven opulent, colorfully themed chambers. Each chamber is illuminated by blood-red firelight filtering through stained glass, creating an eerie, otherworldly atmosphere, while a massive ebony clock in the blackest chamber tolls each hour, momentarily halting the revelry and plunging the guests into dread.\\n\\nAs the night unfolds, the festivities grow more intense, yet the recurring chimes of the ebony clock serve as a grim reminder of time’s inexorable march. At the stroke of midnight, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, with a corpse-like mask and dripping crimson stains. The sight sends shockwaves through the crowd, paralyzing them with fear. Prince Prospero, consumed by fury and a sense of personal affront, draws a dagger and pursues the figure through the seven chambers, driven by a desire to reclaim control over his domain. His pursuit ends in the black room, where he confronts the figure only to collapse dead upon realizing it is empty—revealing the horrifying truth that the plague has infiltrated the abbey all along.\\n\\nIn the final moments, the illusion of safety shatters completely. The revelers, now realizing the futility of their isolation, begin to die one by one, succumbing to the very disease they sought to escape. The abbey, once a sanctuary of decadence and denial, becomes a tomb of silence and decay. The story concludes with the complete annihilation of all who sought refuge within its walls, underscoring the inevitability of death and the futility of attempting to outrun fate. The final image is one of total darkness, where even the memory of revelry fades into the void.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama