r: var(--text);\n            line-height: 1.6;\n            padding: 2rem;\n        }\n\n        .container { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; }\n\n        /* Tab Navigation */\n        nav {\n            position: sticky;\n            top: 0;\n            background: var(--surface);\n            padding: 0;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            margin-bottom: 2rem;\n            z-index: 100;\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 0;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            justify-content: center;\n            overflow: hidden;\n        }\n        nav a {\n            color: var(--text);\n            text-decoration: none;\n            padding: 1rem 1.5rem;\n            transition: all 0.2s;\n            border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            position: relative;\n        }\n        nav a:hover {\n            background: var(--primary);\n        }\n        nav a.active {\n            background: var(--surface-alt);\n            border-bottom-color: var(--accent);\n            color: var(--accent);\n            font-weight: 600;\n        }\n\n        /* Hide all tab content by default, show only active tab */\n        .tab-content {\n            display: none;\n        }\n        .tab-content.active {\n            display: block;\n        }\n\n        /* View toggle buttons */\n        .view-toggle {\n            padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n            border: 1px solid var(--primary);\n            background: transparent;\n            color: var(--text);\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            transition: all 0.2s;\n        }\n        .view-toggle:hover {\n            background: var(--primary);\n        }\n        .view-toggle.active {\n            background: var(--accent);\n            border-color: var(--accent);\n            font-weight: 600;\n        }\n\n        /* Pronunciation views */\n        .pron-view {\n            display: none;\n        }\n        .pron-view.active {\n            display: block;\n        }\n\n        /* Glossary styles */\n        .alphabet-nav a:hover {\n            background: var(--accent) !important;\n        }\n        .glossary-item:hover {\n            background: var(--primary) !important;\n        }\n\n        /* Print view: show all tabs and all pronunciation views */\n        @media print {\n            nav {\n                display: none;\n            }\n            .tab-content {\n                display: block !important;\n                page-break-before: always;\n            }\n            .tab-content:first-of-type {\n                page-break-before: auto;\n            }\n            .view-toggle {\n                display: none !important;\n            }\n            .pron-view {\n                display: block !important;\n                page-break-before: always;\n            }\n            /* Glossary print styles */\n            .alphabet-nav {\n                display: none !important;\n            }\n            #glossary-search, button[onclick=\"clearGlossarySearch()\"] {\n                display: none !important;\n            }\n            #glossary-count {\n                display: none !important;\n            }\n            .glossary-section {\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Mobile responsive tabs */\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            nav {\n                flex-direction: column;\n            }\n            nav a {\n                text-align: center;\n            }\n        }\n\n        header {\n            text-align: center;\n            padding: 2rem;\n            background: var(--surface);\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            margin-bottom: 2rem;\n        }\n\n        header h1 { color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 2.5rem; }\n        header .meta { color: var(--muted); }\n\n        .stats {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));\n            gap: 1rem;\n            margin-bottom: 2rem;\n        }\n\n        .stat-card {\n            background: var(--surface);\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        .stat-card .value {\n            font-size: 2rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: var(--accent);\n        }\n\n        .stat-card .label { color: var(--muted); }\n\n        section {\n            background: var(--surface);\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 2rem;\n        }\n\n        section h2 {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\n            padding-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1rem;\n            font-size: 1.5rem;\n        }\n\n        section h3 {\n            color: var(--accent-soft);\n            margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem 0;\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\n        }\n\n        table {\n            width: 100%;\n            border-collapse: collapse;\n        }\n\n        th, td {\n            padding: 0.75rem;\n            text-align: left;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--primary);\n        }\n\n        th { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }\n\n        tr:hover { background: var(--primary); }\n\n        .tag {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            font-size: 0.85rem;\n            background: var(--primary);\n            margin: 0.1rem;\n        }\n\n        .tag.homograph { background: #5a3d7a; }\n        .tag.proper_noun { background: #3d5a7a; }\n        .tag.foreign { background: #7a5a3d; }\n        .tag.unknown { background: #5a5a5a; }\n        .tag.llm_refined { background: var(--success); }\n        .tag.high { background: var(--success); }\n        .tag.medium { background: var(--warning); }\n        .tag.low { background: #5a2727; }\n\n        /* Confidence badges */\n        .confidence-badge {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            cursor: help;\n            margin-left: 0.5rem;\n        }\n        .confidence-badge.high {\n            background: var(--success);\n            color: #fff;\n        }\n        .confidence-badge.medium {\n            background: var(--warning);\n            color: #333;\n        }\n        .confidence-badge.low {\n            background: #5a2727;\n            color: #fff;\n        }\n\n        .context {\n            font-style: italic;\n            color: var(--muted);\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n        }\n\n        .aliases { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }\n\n        .description {\n            font-style: italic;\n            color: var(--muted);\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n            margin-top: 0.25rem;\n        }\n\n        .warning {\n            background: #5a4a27;\n            padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n        }\n\n        /* Relationship cards */\n        .relationship-grid {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));\n            gap: 1rem;\n        }\n\n        .relationship-card {\n            background: var(--surface-alt);\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            padding: 1rem;\n            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);\n        }\n","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2826}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01QGqNi8MwvNj7f71CmFfZjv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The HTML presentation looks professional and well-structured. Now I have all the information I need to evaluate attempt 15 for \"The Masque of the Red Death\" by Edgar Allan Poe. Let me perform the evaluation.\n\n## Evaluation of \"The Masque of the Red Death\" - Attempt 15\n\n### Ground Truth for this Text\n\n\"The Masque of the Red Death\" is a short story by Edgar Allan Poe with:\n- **Structure**: A single continuous narrative (no chapter divisions in the original)\n- **Expected Characters**:\n  - **Prince Prospero** - The protagonist, a wealthy prince who isolates himself from the plague\n  - **The Red Death / The Masked Figure / The Mummer** - The antagonist, a supernatural personification of the plague who appears at the masquerade. This is NOT Prince Prospero.\n  - Supporting cast: Courtiers/revelers (unnamed group)\n\n**Critical Plot Point**: Prince Prospero DIES after confronting the mummer. The mummer kills Prospero. They are definitively TWO SEPARATE ENTITIES.\n\n---\n\n### 2.1 Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\n\n**Expected**: This is a short story with no chapter divisions - it's a single continuous narrative.\n**Actual**: 1 chapter detected\n\n**Score: 10/10**\n\nThis is correct. The story has no internal chapter structure, and the tool correctly identified it as a single unit.\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\n\n**Expected Characters**:\n1. Prince Prospero (protagonist)\n2. The Red Death / The Mummer / The Masked Figure (antagonist)\n\n**Actual Output**:\n- 1 character: \"the Prince Prospero\" with aliases [\"Prospero\", \"the mummer\"]\n\n**CRITICAL FAILURE**: The mummer (the Red Death personification) is incorrectly listed as an alias of Prince Prospero. This is catastrophically wrong:\n\n1. **Prince Prospero is the VICTIM** - \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\"\n2. **The mummer KILLS Prince Prospero** - They cannot be the same character\n3. **The mummer is revealed to be empty/supernatural** - \"untenanted by any tangible form\"\n4. **They have a physical confrontation** - Prospero pursues the mummer through 7 chambers\n\nThe chapter summary CORRECTLY identifies them as separate:\n> \"Prince Prospero... pursues the figure through the chambers with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black room\"\n\nBut the character extraction merged them.\n\n**Missing Character**: The Red Death/Masked Figure/Mummer should be its own entry with aliases.\n\n**Missing Alias**: \"the duke\" for Prince Prospero (text says \"The tastes of the duke were peculiar\")\n\n**Minor Issue**: Canonical name includes article (\"the Prince Prospero\" vs \"Prince Prospero\")\n\n**Score: 3/10**\n\nThe main antagonist of the story is merged with the protagonist. This is a fundamental failure.\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n\n**Prince Prospero's Profile**:\n- Description is largely accurate for Prospero himself\n- Evidence quotes are correct\n- But the profile contains evidence that PROVES these are separate characters:\n  > \"He collapses and dies upon confronting the figure in the black room\"\n  > \"The figure is revealed to be empty, wearing grave cerements and a corpse-like mask\"\n\nThe profile contradicts the alias merge by showing Prospero dies while the mummer continues to exist.\n\n**Score: 6/10**\n\nThe profile content is reasonable for Prospero, but the fundamental character identification error undermines it.\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n\n**Chapter 1 Summary Review**:\n- ✅ Correctly describes the Red Death plague\n- ✅ Correctly describes Prospero's isolation strategy\n- ✅ Correctly describes the seven colored chambers\n- ✅ Correctly describes the ebony clock\n- ✅ Correctly identifies \"Prince Prospero\" and \"the figure\" as separate entities in confrontation\n- ✅ Correctly notes Prospero's death\n- ✅ Correctly notes the figure is \"empty\" / \"untenanted\"\n\nThe summary is accurate and well-written. Notably, it correctly treats Prospero and the masked figure as separate entities, which contradicts the character extraction.\n\n**Score: 9/10**\n\n---\n\n### 2.5 Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n\n**Good flagging**:\n- Prospero ✅ (proper noun, correct IPA)\n- mummer ✅ (archaic term)\n- improvisatori ✅ (Italian origin)\n- habiliments ✅ (archaic)\n- cerements ✅ (archaic)\n- Hernani ✅ (literary reference)\n- arabesque ✅ (loan word)\n\n**False positives** (common English words that don't need pronunciation help):\n- Prince (standard English)\n- chiming (common word)\n- magnificence (common word)\n- dauntless (common word)\n- buffoons (common word)\n- casements (common word)\n- evolutions (common word)\n- light-hearted (compound, obvious pronunciation)\n- glaringly (common word)\n- fire-light (compound, obvious pronunciation)\n- blood-tinted (compound, obvious pronunciation)\n- etc.\n\nI count approximately 25-30 false positives out of 73 entries (~35-40% false positive rate).\n\n**Incorrect foreign word flagging**:\n- \"decorum\" flagged as foreign - it's standard English (Latin-derived but fully assimilated for centuries)\n\n**Score: 6/10**\n\nGood coverage of genuinely unusual words, but too many common words flagged.\n\n---\n\n### 2.6 HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n\n- ✅ Clean, professional dark theme\n- ✅ Tab-based navigation\n- ✅ Responsive design (mobile CSS present)\n- ✅ Print styles included\n- ✅ Color-coded confidence badges\n- ✅ Proper structure with sections\n- ✅ View toggle functionality\n\n**Score: 8/10**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Calculate Overall Score\n\n```\nOverall = (\n    Structure × 0.20 +     10 × 0.20 = 2.00\n    Characters × 0.25 +     3 × 0.25 = 0.75\n    Profiles × 0.15 +       6 × 0.15 = 0.90\n    Summaries × 0.20 +      9 × 0.20 = 1.80\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +  6 × 0.10 = 0.60\n    Presentation × 0.10     8 ×