{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_014LmFup3iNpjukt9Rm3sxQ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Evaluation Complete\n\n**Result: FAIL (6.85/10)**\n\n### Summary\n\nAttempt 15 tried to fix the \"mummer\" / \"Prince Prospero\" merge by increasing the pairwise context window from 160-200 chars to 250-300 chars. The theory was that the death scene evidence (~221 chars) was being truncated before reaching the LLM.\n\n**Findings:**\n- **Smoke test PASSED** - showed 2 separate characters\n- **Full analysis FAILED** - characters still merged\n\nThis discrepancy suggests the problem is not purely about context length. The LLM behavior may vary between runs, or other pipeline factors are influencing the merge decision.\n\n### Key Observation\nThe chapter summary pipeline **correctly** identifies \"Prince Prospero\" and \"the masked figure (Red Death)\" as two separate entities, proving the underlying LLM can distinguish them. The character extraction pipeline is the specific bottleneck.\n\n### Recommended Next Approach\nSince 15 pre-merge approaches have failed, I recommend a **POST-PROCESSING** approach:\n\n1. After character extraction completes, scan merged characters for death relationship evidence\n2. If one alias \"dies\" while another \"kills\" them, force-split into separate characters\n3. Alternatively, compare character list against `characters_present` from summaries to detect false merges\n\nThe loop will continue with `PROMPT_fix.md` to implement the next fix attempt."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":74467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe15f172-7bd8-48af-b88c-b00d2214dcbf","uuid":"f974512b-9770-4165-a2c2-e7563b4925c5"}
